3. Sequence — bounds check vs. memcpy: check `if ((pnt + hdr->length + 3) > end)` (line 43) ensures only total-message bounds; it never verifies `hdr->length >= sizeof(struct capability_mp_data)`. Then `memcpy(&mpc, pnt + 3, sizeof (struct capability_mp_data))` (line 49) reads a fixed-size stack buffer from `pnt+3`.
