4. Sequence (line 63-64): `len = (int)(p - *arg + extra); rettv->vval.v_string = alloc(len);` — `extra` is approximate, not exact expanded length.
5. Loop (line 69): `for (p = *arg + off; *p != NUL && *p != '"'; )` — writes to `end` with no pre-write bounds check against `len`.
6. Branch (line 73): `switch (*++p)` — after increment `p` can point to NUL if input ends with `\`; then hex branch (line 82-85: `if (vim_isxdigit(p[1]))`) reads `p[1]` past buffer.
